# Trivy ignore list for the contextmatrix-agent worker-image scan.
#
# The worker-image-scan job fails on CRITICAL/HIGH vulnerabilities that have an
# upstream fix (ignore-unfixed: true). Every entry must carry a justification;
# review on each worker-image / Go-dependency bump and delete entries whose fix
# has shipped. Dependabot (.github/dependabot.yml) tracks the underlying bumps.

# --- The bundled npm CLI (12.2.0, the latest release) ships brace-expansion
# 5.0.9 (/usr/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/brace-expansion); the fixes land
# in 5.0.10 and 5.0.11. DoS via crafted brace patterns inside the npm CLI - the
# single-tenant worker only expands globs npm generates itself. npm's own
# transitive dependency - clears when an npm release pulls in >= 5.0.11.
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278

# --- The bundled npm CLI (12.2.0) ships undici 6.28.0
# (/usr/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/undici); the fix is 6.28.1. DoS via an
# unrequested WebSocket subprotocol - npm speaks plain HTTPS to the registry and
# opens no WebSockets. npm's own transitive dependency - clears when an npm
# release pulls in undici >= 6.28.1.
CVE-2026-19534

# --- The uv-managed CPython (/opt/python) bundles pip, whose _vendor tree pins
# msgpack==1.1.2 and setuptools==70.3.0 (pip/_vendor/vendor.txt - Trivy reads
# the pins as installed packages). GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 (msgpack Unpacker-reuse
# out-of-bounds read, fixed in 1.2.1) touches only pip's deserialization of its
# own local HTTP cache. CVE-2025-47273 (setuptools PackageIndex path traversal,
# fixed in 78.1.1) lives in package_index.py, which pip's vendored copy does not
# ship - only the pkg_resources subset of setuptools is vendored. The pins
# cannot be raised independently of pip, and the latest pip (26.2.1) still
# carries both - clears when a pip release re-vendors msgpack >= 1.2.1 and
# setuptools >= 78.1.1.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273

# --- The same pip vendor tree pins urllib3==2.7.0; the fixes land in 2.8.0.
# CVE-2026-97687 (HTTPS-proxy TLS configuration override) needs a configured
# HTTPS proxy, which the worker does not set; CVE-2026-97689 (unbounded chunk
# allocation) is a DoS against pip's own index downloads on a single-tenant
# worker that already runs repo-controlled code. pip 26.2.1 still vendors
# 2.7.0 - clears when a pip release re-vendors urllib3 >= 2.8.0.
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
